# Welfare Benefit Pattern Mining & Youth Support Region Prediction

> Association Rule Mining and Logistic Regression applied to Australia's DSS SA2 Demographics Dataset using R

---

## Overview

This project applies data mining techniques to the **Department of Social Services (DSS) Payment Demographics** dataset to:

- Discover hidden co-occurrence patterns among welfare benefit types across Australian SA2 regions
- Predict regions with high Youth Allowance (student and apprentice) recipients using Logistic Regression

The study leverages R programming and a suite of visualization tools to enhance understanding of social service distributions and support data-driven welfare planning in Australia.

